    "recommendations": "Reducing direct vegetation contact with the structure by creating and maintaining separation between combustible shrubs, brush, and tree clusters and the building perimeter could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity in the immediate structure zone. Managing scattered trees and mixed vegetation cover to increase spacing between individual plants and canopy layers may reduce opportunities for fire to move through connected fuels toward improvements. Removing or thinning brush and shrubs that are directly adjacent to the structure would further support defensible space within the near-structure perimeter. Maintaining and expanding the existing open fuel break could support suppression operations and reduce fuel continuity across the property. Continued management of vegetation growing along the access route would support firefighter access and improve navigation during emergency response. Preserving and expanding the irrigated landscape near the structure may reduce fuel availability in the immediate perimeter and contribute to long-term wildfire resilience."
